    <!--
      Tab-row label size. commons' big_text_size is 18sp; the 1.0.7 spec asked for +2, and the
      1.0.9 spec asks for another +2 on top of what shipped, so it is pinned locally rather than
      changing a library value that is used elsewhere.
    -->
    <dimen name="main_tab_text_size">20sp</dimen>

    <!--
      Geometry of the thread bottom bar's operator badge (1.1.07 spec).

      The width is `wrap_content`, so the operator name (移动 / 联通 / 电信, or 移动1 / 移动2) is
      what sizes the card - that is the fix for the fixed-width icon the label used to spill out
      of. The HEIGHT stays fixed at `sim_badge_height` so a one-digit label and a three-character
      one are the same size.
      🔴 24dp is deliberate: it matches the icon it replaced. The first 1.1.07 attempt reused
      `normal_icon_size` (48dp) for both axes, which turned the chip into a full-height block that
      filled the whole bottom bar.

      `sim_badge_horizontal_padding` is the inner gap on each side of the label; it mirrors
      `SimBadgeSpan.PAD_RATIO` on the message metadata line.
    -->
    <dimen name="sim_badge_height">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="sim_badge_horizontal_padding">6dp</dimen>
</resources>
